sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor H as Release team
    participant G as Shared Git repository
    participant C as Argo CD
    participant R as Argo Rollouts
    participant S as Service Mesh
    participant M as Monitoring

    Note over H,M: ROLLBACK - v2 fails during its canary, before promotion. Stable v1 is still available
    Note over C,M: These components belong to the affected OpenShift site

    R->>M: Request canary health measurements
    M-->>R: Return unhealthy measurements
    R->>R: Configured failure threshold is exceeded
    R->>R: Automatically abort the local canary
    R->>S: Restore 100% of local Orders traffic to stable v1
    S->>S: Apply the restored traffic policy
    Note over G,S: Traffic recovery is automatic. Git still declares v2
    H->>H: Verify service recovery and hold further release approvals

    H->>G: Open a PR restoring only the affected site's version to v1
    H->>G: Review and merge the recovery PR
    C->>G: Fetch the approved recovery configuration
    G-->>C: Desired application version is v1
    C->>R: Sync the previous stable version
    R->>R: Reconcile v1 as the desired stable release
    H->>C: Verify application is Synced and Healthy
    C-->>H: Git and running application agree on v1

    Note over C,M: Other site stays unchanged. If A fails, B stays on v1. If B fails, A stays on v2
    Note over H,S: GTM site distribution stays unchanged. Investigate v2 before approving another release

